hops.notes:
Kept only candidates whose intended solution matches the query’s key pipeline: (1) convert a binomial/hypergeometric/elliptic object into an integral representation; (2) generate higher powers in (n+1)^{-k} (or log^k) via Beta/log integrals or parameter differentiation; (3) reduce to polylog/elliptic-type integrals that evaluate to combinations involving log 2, π, and especially Catalan’s constant via arctan/1+x^2 kernels or complete elliptic integrals K. 

Why the others were rejected: many are (i) purely log/polylog integrals giving ζ-values or π^4 without the elliptic/central-binomial/2F1(1/2,1/2;1;z) bridge; (ii) finite binomial/Catalan convolution identities solved by generating functions or combinatorics (no log-Beta integral + elliptic step); (iii) multi-integrals leading to Gamma/zeta identities rather than Catalan/elliptic constants; or (iv) analytic-number-theory identities unrelated to the central-binomial/elliptic mechanism.

What analogues are still missing: closer structural matches that explicitly feature the same coefficient sequence (2n choose n)^2/16^n or 2F1(1/2,1/2;1;z) and a (n+1)^{-k} (or harmonic-number / polylog-weight) factor, whose evaluation forces the “interchange sum–integral → elliptic integral K(z) → special-value reduction” step and produces G. Good next-hop targets: 
- series of the form Σ (2nCn)^2/16^n * H_n/(n+1)^2 or Σ (2nCn)^2/16^n /(n+1)^m for m=1,2,4; 
- integrals with K(k) or K(k)^2 multiplied by log terms or arctan terms (log-power generating the cubic denominator); 
- problems using the substitution z = 4x(1-x) / Landen transformations to evaluate K-related integrals at k=1/√2, where G naturally appears.

